# Go coverage profile (build artifact)
coverage-go.out

# Secret material -- narrowed to filename shapes that genuinely hold
# credentials, not any path containing the substring "secret". The old
# blanket `*secret*` glob matched on name only, not content, so it could
# not tell a credential file from prose about one: it blocked legitimate
# Helm Secret/ExternalSecret chart *templates* (k8s/helm/**/templates/
# secret.yaml, externalsecret.yaml -- no real secret material, template
# syntax only) and, worse, silently untracked tests/api/test_secret_key.py
# -- a test *about* secret handling, ignored without any error, which is
# indistinguishable from a test that was never written. Content-based
# detection (gitleaks, detect-private-key -- both in the pre-commit hooks)
# is the real control against committed secret material; this glob is
# belt-and-braces for the predictable filename shapes credentials
# actually take. Narrowed this way, the Helm templates above no longer
# match, so no negation exception is needed for them.
*.secret
*.secrets
secrets.env
secrets/
*-secrets.yaml
*-secrets.yml
